== ECON 0100 Syllabus Quiz

~

+ What primarily determines your final course grade? \
  ( ) Your average across homework and Checkpoints \
  (X) The percentage of assessed skills you pass \
  ( ) Your performance relative to other students \
  ( ) Attendance and participation
+ Suppose you pass 94% of the assessed skills. What is your final letter grade? \
  ( ) A+ \
  (X) A \
  ( ) A- \
  ( ) It depends on the class average
+ A skill that you have already passed can become a no-pass because of a lower score on a later reattempt. \
  ( ) True \
  (X) False
+ Which are the three types of practice for each skill? Select all that apply. \
  \[X\] Exercises completed in class \
  \[X\] Vignettes completed in recitation \
  \[X\] Homework \
  \[ \] Reading quizzes \
  \[ \] Discussion posts
+ How much practice must you complete to unlock your first attempt at a skill? \
  ( ) Any one of the three practice types \
  (X) Two of the three practice types \
  ( ) All three practice types \
  ( ) Practice is recommended but does not affect eligibility
+ How much practice must you complete to unlock a reattempt at a skill? \
  ( ) One of the three practice types \
  ( ) Two of the three practice types \
  (X) All three practice types \
  ( ) Only the practice type you missed previously
+ Jordan completed the Exercise and Homework for a skill but missed its Vignette. Which statement is correct? \
  (X) Jordan may take the first attempt but has not yet unlocked a reattempt. \
  ( ) Jordan may not take the first attempt. \
  ( ) Jordan has unlocked both the first attempt and a reattempt. \
  ( ) Jordan automatically receives a no-pass for the skill.
+ Priya has unlocked some, but not all, of the skills appearing on an upcoming Checkpoint. What should she do? \
  ( ) Skip the entire Checkpoint. \
  (X) Take the Checkpoint and answer only the skills she has unlocked. \
  ( ) Answer every skill but expect a grade penalty. \
  ( ) Request a separate version of the Checkpoint.
+ Marcus missed practice and therefore did not unlock a skill before its Checkpoint. When may he make up that practice? \
  ( ) Immediately before the Checkpoint begins \
  ( ) During the Checkpoint \
  (X) After the Checkpoint, in preparation for the next Reattempt \
  ( ) Missed practice can never be made up
+ Which materials may you use during a Checkpoint or Reattempt? Select all that apply. \
  \[X\] Your nonelectronic notes \
  \[X\] A nonelectronic copy of the textbook \
  \[X\] A calculator \
  \[ \] Notes stored on your phone \
  \[ \] An online AI assistant \
  \[ \] Electronic textbook materials on a laptop
+ Homework and other practice are graded primarily for correctness. \
  ( ) True \
  (X) False
+ Which statement best describes collaboration on homework? \
  ( ) It is prohibited. \
  ( ) It is permitted but discouraged. \
  (X) It is strongly encouraged. \
  ( ) It is allowed only with written permission.
+ Which statement best represents the course's AI policy? \
  ( ) AI use is completely prohibited throughout the course. \
  ( ) AI may complete Checkpoints as long as the student cites it. \
  (X) The course does not prohibit AI, but students are encouraged to do Homework without its direct aid so they develop the skills they must demonstrate themselves. \
  ( ) Students are required to use AI on every Homework assignment.
+ What happens during the Final Exam Period? \
  ( ) Only a cumulative traditional final exam \
  ( ) Checkpoint F only \
  ( ) A reattempt session only \
  (X) Checkpoint F and a reattempt session
+ Which platform-purpose pairings are correct? Select all that apply. \
  \[X\] Canvas — Records passed skills and contains announcements \
  \[X\] Gradescope — Collects and returns assignments \
  \[X\] Course website — Provides the Skillsheet, videos, Homework, Demos, and office-hour information \
  \[ \] Canvas — Serves as the primary portal for submitting and receiving assignments \
  \[ \] Gradescope — Lists every assessed skill and its standard \
  \[ \] Course website — Determines students' final letter grades
+ Your grade may be curved downward if the rest of the class performs especially well. \
  ( ) True \
  (X) False
+ A student no-passes two skills on a Checkpoint. Before the next Reattempt, the student completes all three required practice types for those skills. What must the student redo? \
  ( ) The entire Checkpoint \
  (X) Only the skills the student has not yet passed \
  ( ) Every skill from the current course part \
  ( ) Nothing, because Checkpoint results cannot change
+ Which consequences may result from academic dishonesty? Select all that apply. \
  \[X\] Failing all skills assessed on the Checkpoint in question with no reattempt \
  \[X\] Receiving an F in the course \
  \[ \] Losing only five participation points \
  \[ \] Receiving an automatic warning with no other consequences
  
